WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:04.845
George and Mabel lived on a small farm.

2
00:00:04.846 --> 00:00:09.379
Though they had little, they were happy.

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:15.553
But one year the weather was hot and dry.

4
00:00:15.554 --> 00:00:19.472
Very few crops grew.

5
00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:24.403
Even their last chicken died.

6
00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:29.308
George looked at the vegetables and sighed.

7
00:00:29.309 --> 00:00:32.994
"We don't have much to sell at the market this year.

8
00:00:32.995 --> 00:00:36.628
That means a very hard winter, Mabel."

9
00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:42.554
Mabel looked nervous. "I hope we'll be okay."

10
00:00:42.555 --> 00:00:48.674
At the market George sold his vegetables for a few coins.

11
00:00:48.675 --> 00:00:56.244
By the time he reached home, he was even more worried.

12
00:00:56.245 --> 00:01:03.547
"This money will not last long," he thought.

13
00:01:03.548 --> 00:01:05.156
Honk!

14
00:01:05.157 --> 00:01:07.538
"What's that?" George thought.

15
00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:08.795
Honk!

16
00:01:08.796 --> 00:01:13.502
George followed the noise to the empty chicken coop.

17
00:01:13.503 --> 00:01:16.155
He saw a goose.

18
00:01:16.156 --> 00:01:20.199
"Where did you come from?" George asked.

19
00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:24.277
Just then something shiny caught his eye.

20
00:01:24.278 --> 00:01:26.945
George looked in the coop.

21
00:01:26.946 --> 00:01:29.623
He saw an egg.

22
00:01:29.624 --> 00:01:33.262
He picked it up, and his eyes went wide.

23
00:01:33.263 --> 00:01:38.953
It wasn't just any egg—it was a golden egg!

24
00:01:38.954 --> 00:01:42.813
"Mabel!" he cried as he ran inside.

25
00:01:42.814 --> 00:01:45.628
"We don't have to worry anymore!"

26
00:01:45.629 --> 00:01:51.203
Mabel looked at him, confused. "What?"

27
00:01:51.204 --> 00:01:53.817
George showed her the egg.

28
00:01:53.818 --> 00:01:56.887
Tears of joy filled Mabel's eyes.

29
00:01:56.888 --> 00:02:02.052
"We'll have food and fuel for the winter."

30
00:02:02.053 --> 00:02:05.905
The next day the goose laid another golden egg. George

31
00:02:05.906 --> 00:02:08.682
was thrilled. "If

32
00:02:08.683 --> 00:02:12.711
the goose lays more golden eggs, we'll be rich! You

33
00:02:12.712 --> 00:02:15.277
can buy new clothes! We

34
00:02:15.278 --> 00:02:18.223
can build a huge house." "Now,

35
00:02:18.224 --> 00:02:21.169
now," Mabel said. "We

36
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:24.129
don't need any of that. We've

37
00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:27.054
lived just fine the way we are. These

38
00:02:27.055 --> 00:02:31.695
two eggs will be a huge help." That

39
00:02:31.696 --> 00:02:35.779
night George kept thinking of the goose. Surely

40
00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:40.189
it would lay more golden eggs. "I

41
00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.039
could get jewels for Mabel," he thought. "And

42
00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.141
some fancy shoes for myself, and . . ." George

43
00:02:47.142 --> 00:02:49.704
sat up in bed. "I'll

44
00:02:49.705 --> 00:02:52.863
open the goose's belly! Then

45
00:02:52.864 --> 00:02:56.842
I can get all the eggs at once!" George

46
00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.185
slipped outside. Inside

47
00:02:59.186 --> 00:03:02.787
the coop, the goose was sleeping. George

48
00:03:02.788 --> 00:03:07.035
reached for the goose, and— Honk! Honk!

49
00:03:07.036 --> 00:03:11.618
Suddenly the goose bit George's arm.

50
00:03:11.619 --> 00:03:15.158
"Ouch!" George cried.

51
00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:20.453
The goose flapped its wings and chased George. Honk! Honk!

52
00:03:20.454 --> 00:03:23.570
George tripped and fell on his face.

53
00:03:23.571 --> 00:03:28.352
When he looked up, he saw the goose flying away.

54
00:03:28.353 --> 00:03:34.465
Mabel ran outside. "What's going on?"

55
00:03:34.466 --> 00:03:37.532
George told Mabel what happened.

56
00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:40.485
He hung his head in shame.

57
00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.931
"The goose could have helped us a lot.

58
00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:48.263
But now, because of me, we lost it."

59
00:03:48.264 --> 00:03:50.863
Mabel sighed.

60
00:03:50.864 --> 00:03:58.930
"Oh, George. Bad things happen when people become greedy."

